  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coastal States Stability Mechanism (CSSM)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Coastal States Stability Mechanism (CSSM) contributes to government strategies by creatin conditions for stronger and locally accepted state presence that is responsive to community priorities. To achieve its objectives, the CSSM will work in limited number of geographic zones selected based on government security and stabilization priorities. In each location, CSSM will work with government and community partners under three stabilization outcomes relating to (1) critical civil security services, (2) essential social services, and (3) social and economic engagements. These outcomes are interlinked, as the first creates an enabling environment to pursue the second and third, and the three act together to counter VEO expansion. The CSSM will foster national leadership and unity of effort across civilian, security and community actors through collaborative processes for analysis, planning, priotization, and implementation, which will be articulated in Integrated Community Stabilization Approaches (ICSA). These are co-developed at the local level by community and government (civilian and security) stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
